From 0d8a7b4376d9345e452c3ff4cfd3310588002ff6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:00:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] port 038994f4 aeb0cc4f: verify: QSA slots launches with a
 streamed KV cache when every row is another slot's (opt-in
 STRATA_QSA_SLOTS_STREAM=1)

Each row resolves its own map after the rows' top-k and before their attention. Test qsa_slots_stream_parity
compares slots-with-streaming against the per-row loop bitwise, with evictions (aeb0cc4f folded in: the test syncs
after zeroing, and says why on an attention mismatch).

(cherry picked from commits 038994f4e235 and aeb0cc4f230c)

Port to v0.2.12:
- the switch is read at first use like upstream's qsa_slots_on() (qsa_slots_stream_on()), so values that main()
  sets before the first window are seen.
- v0.2.12 put STRATA_BATCH_ATTN_ROWS in front of the slots branch; that branch still excludes streamed KV, so a
  streamed window reaches the slots branch, which now also takes it when rows_own_slots.  The per-row resolve
  goes between qsa_block_topk and qsa_decode_attn_slots as before; when the slots launcher declines, the per-row
  attention fallback runs after the resolves (same order as the per-row loop for rows of distinct slots).
- new: a told-once line per path, "strata verify: batch decode attention: rows | slots | slots-stream | per-row |
  daily", plus the STRATA_ATTN_DAILY value.  On sm_86 v0.2.12's defaults set STRATA_ATTN_DAILY=1, which makes
  qsa_decode_attn_slots() decline (pre75_attn()), so STRATA_QSA_SLOTS(_STREAM) silently ran per-row launches; the
  line shows which path a build/arm really runs.  Printed when a window graph is recorded, not per launch.
- ctest qsa_slots_stream_parity(_lanecell) pins STRATA_ATTN_DAILY=0 (with the Daily's kernel the slots launcher
  declines and the test would only skip).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
